---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-drip';
const title = 'Yotpo Email & SMS vs Drip for Shopify: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Moving from retired Yotpo Email & SMS to Drip: purchase events, reorder branches, review ownership and workflow migration checks.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I still choose Yotpo Email & SMS?",
    "answer": "No. Yotpo scheduled Email and SMS retirement for December 31, 2025. Its current SMS notice confirms that the dashboard and background services are decommissioned."
  },
  {
    "question": "What Shopify data does Drip document?",
    "answer": "Its connection guide covers customer, order and product sync, plus site tracking through the app embed. Inspect your actual records before rebuilding branches."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will Shopify sync restore old Yotpo workflows?",
    "answer": "No. Destination order data does not contain the old workflow definitions. Reconstruct conditions, delays and exclusions from retained configuration records."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I keep review collection separate?",
    "answer": "Yes, plan separate ownership for review collection and lifecycle email. Any branch that depends on review completion needs an established data path; this page does not establish a native Yotpo Reviews bridge."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does a reorder workflow prove a subscription integration?",
    "answer": "No. A purchase event is different from a subscription renewal, pause or cancellation. Map those states from the subscription system before using them in automation."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I compare cost and alternatives?",
    "answer": "Request a current quote for the actual audience and sends, then include SMS, reviews and integration maintenance. Sequenzy can be another candidate, but no price or workflow advantage is established here."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-cyan-100/90">/</span>
        <span class="text-cyan-100/90">Yotpo Email & SMS vs Drip</span>
      </nav>

<header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="badge">Migration comparison</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS vs Drip for Shopify</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9 text-cyan-100">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS is retired. For a Shopify team considering Drip, the practical question is how to rebuild editable email workflows from retained records, while assigning review, loyalty and SMS responsibilities separately. This guide proposes checks; it reports no merchant trials or measured improvements.</p></header>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Start from the retirement boundary</h2>
<p>Yotpo announced the retirement of Email and SMS. Its current SMS notice says account dashboards and background services are inactive. Inventory exports and workflow notes already held by the store; ask support about any recovery route without assuming access remains. Retaining Yotpo Reviews or Loyalty does not restore the discontinued sender.</p>
<h2>Connect data before recreating logic</h2>
<p>Drip documents Shopify customer, order and product synchronization. Its app embed supplies site tracking. Complete the connection and inspect representative records before enabling workflows. Separate an imported customer from a person eligible for marketing, and preserve the origin of any retained subscription or suppression record.</p>
<h2>Choose the event at the right level</h2>
<p>Drip documents both order-level and item-level purchase events. For a mixed basket, decide whether the workflow should start once for the order or separately for each relevant item. Record the event name, product identifier and deduplication rule in the workflow notes. Do not attach the same thank-you message to both levels without checking for duplicate entry.</p>
<h2>Proposed scenario: variable snack-box replenishment</h2>
<p>For a hypothetical snack-box store, distinguish a one-off gift, a repeat household purchase and an active subscription. Start with the actual product identifiers and purchase date available in the connected record. Use a timing assumption agreed by the operator rather than claiming to know consumption. If box size is only a Shopify metafield, verify that it reaches a usable Drip field; the basic connection guide does not prove that mapping.</p>
<h2>Subscription state needs its own source</h2>
<p>A replenishment prompt may be inappropriate for a buyer whose subscription is already scheduled. Define where active, paused and cancelled status originates and how it updates. If that source is unavailable, hold the subscription-dependent branch or use content that does not imply knowledge of the next shipment. A tag left over from migration is not proof of a current subscription.</p>
<h2>Proposed welcome and exclusion check</h2>
<p>Create controlled records for a footer signup, a gift buyer and a wholesale-tagged buyer. Inspect the available source and exclusion fields before connecting them to welcome branches. Confirm that an unsubscribed customer stays outside promotional delivery. Keep wholesale quote follow-up separate unless its source data is demonstrated; do not infer it from an order feed.</p>
<h2>Proposed recovery and purchase-exit check</h2>
<p>Exercise a controlled checkout followed by a purchase. Inspect which event enters recovery, which identifies the cart or items, and which exits the person after payment. Review surviving Shopify recovery and any separate SMS workflow so each message has an owner. These are proposed acceptance checks, not recovery-rate results or evidence that an integration has been tested.</p>
<h2>Keep reviews and loyalty explicit</h2>
<p>List the sender and trigger for care instructions, review requests, points notices and replenishment. When a Drip branch depends on review submission or points status, establish the data source, update delay and responsible maintainer. Otherwise keep that responsibility in the retained service and avoid copy implying that Drip knows a review was completed. This preserves the original comparison’s useful integration question without claiming native suite behavior.</p>
<h2>Make edits safe for the next operator</h2>
<p>For each branch, retain a plain-language entry rule, exit rule, exclusion reason and controlled example. Before changing a replenishment delay, inspect people already waiting in the workflow and establish how the editor handles them. Use a reversible activation plan with the old message owner documented. Do not promise a migration duration or a revenue improvement from canvas visibility.</p>
<h2>Compare the operated program</h2>
<p>Ask Drip for a quote covering the intended audience, send pattern and required functionality. Add the retained review service, any separate SMS service and time to maintain subscription or review mappings. Compare another sender such as Sequenzy against those same concrete requirements. Choose only after demonstrating the event and exclusion paths that make this store unusual, rather than selecting a universal workflow winner.</p>
<h2>Primary evidence and limits</h2><p>Supplier documentation checked November 24, 2026. It documents product scope, not a completed store migration or guaranteed recovery of retired account data.</p><ul><li><a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo retirement announcement</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo end-of-life notice</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://help.drip.com/hc/en-us/articles/4424695491725-Connect-Your-Shopify-Store">Drip Shopify connection</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://help.drip.com/hc/en-us/articles/4424710485261-Shopify-Purchase-Events">Drip purchase events</a></li></ul></article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-drip">Omnisend vs Drip</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-drip">Sequenzy vs Drip</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend">Yotpo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/food-and-beverage">Email apps for food & beverage</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/subscription-boxes">Email apps for subscription boxes</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Yotpo Email &amp; SMS vs Drip FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
